    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n426" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">accūsātrix</span></b> ,
			īcis, f.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>she
				who makes accusation against any one</i>, <i>a
				female accuser</i> (v. accuso <i>no.</i> I.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tu mi accusatrix ades,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. As. 3, 1, 10</span></i>
			; so <i><span class="en">Plin. Ep. 10, 67</span></i>; cf.
					<i><span class="en">Prisc. Op. Min. 102</span></i>
		Lind.</div>
